1
00:00:02,711 --> 00:00:04,880
Hi.

2
00:00:04,922 --> 00:00:06,423
Hey.
Hey.

3
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:08,801
So, what's the final head count
on my baby shower?

4
00:00:08,843 --> 00:00:10,427
About 20.
A couple people from work

5
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:11,762
who had something else to do.

6
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:12,888
Both of your
sisters called

7
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:13,973
and neither can make it.

8
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,808
What? You mean
they're not coming

9
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:18,811
to a social event where
there's no men and no booze?

10
00:00:18,853 --> 00:00:20,103
That's shocking!

11
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:22,272
Well, I don't care.

12
00:00:22,314 --> 00:00:23,440
As long as my mom's here.

13
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:25,943
Oh, my God-- your mother.

14
00:00:25,985 --> 00:00:27,569
What, my mom's
not going to be here?

15
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:29,697
Well, given that
we forgot to invite her

16
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:32,449
it would be an awfully big
coincidence if she was.

17
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:34,827
My God!

18
00:00:34,869 --> 00:00:35,995
It wasn't my fault.

19
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,287
Phoebe was in charge
of invitations.

20
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:39,247
Well, I don't,
I don't have a mother

21
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,708
so often I forget that...

22
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:41,834
Oh, give it a rest.

23
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:46,171
So, my mother is not coming
to my baby shower?

24
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:47,840
No.

25
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:49,633
Neither is mine.

26
00:00:50,968 --> 00:00:51,969
Hey, you know what?

27
00:00:52,011 --> 00:00:52,970
Don't worry, okay?

28
00:00:53,012 --> 00:00:54,013
We'll take care of it.

29
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:55,055
We'll call her.

30
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,431
You just go home
and get ready.

31
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,641
Please make sure
she comes.

32
00:00:57,683 --> 00:00:58,976
It's really important
to me.

33
00:00:59,018 --> 00:01:00,185
I mean, it's my mom.

34
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:01,311
I know, I know.
What's her number?

35
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:03,188
I don't know.

36
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:04,648
Go. I have it in my book.

37
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:05,774
Go.

38
00:01:05,816 --> 00:01:07,150
( door shuts )

39
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,156
Wait a minute.

40
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:14,616
If you're in charge
of invitations

41
00:01:14,658 --> 00:01:16,618
why am I the one
who has to call her?

42
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,703
Hello, Mrs. Green.

43
00:01:17,745 --> 00:01:19,204
Hi. Uh, it's Monica Geller.

44
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:21,040
Oh, hello, Monica.

45
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,875
Hi, um,
I know this is last minute

46
00:01:22,917 --> 00:01:25,168
but we've decided to throw
an impromptu

47
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,128
baby shower
for Rachel today.

48
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,714
I know.

49
00:01:28,756 --> 00:01:30,507
My daughters told me about it
when they received

50
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:32,467
their impromptu invitations
a month ago.

51
00:01:32,509 --> 00:01:33,886
( weak chuckle )

52
00:01:33,928 --> 00:01:35,262
Okay, I'm sorry.

53
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:36,555
I-I'm so sorry.

54
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:37,932
For what, dear?

55
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:40,183
For not inviting me,
or for lying about it?

56
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:44,103
Oh, my God, my ass is sweating.

57
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,232
Oh, please, please...

58
00:01:47,274 --> 00:01:48,316
can you come?

59
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:49,568
It's today at 4:00.

60
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:50,945
Well, all right.

61
00:01:50,986 --> 00:01:52,863
I'll see you at 4:00.

62
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:54,155
Thank you.

63
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:56,366
Isn't it at 3:00?

64
00:01:56,408 --> 00:01:58,493
Son of a bitch!

65
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:10,547
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

66
00:02:10,589 --> 00:02:12,841
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

67
00:02:12,883 --> 00:02:15,886
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

68
00:02:15,928 --> 00:02:19,765
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

69
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:22,059
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

70
00:02:22,101 --> 00:02:24,352
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

71
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:28,607
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

72
00:02:28,649 --> 00:02:32,111
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

73
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,368
Hey, Joe,
want to shoot some hoops?

74
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:41,620
Oh, I can't go.

75
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:42,704
I'm practicing.

76
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:43,831
I got an audition

77
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:45,206
to be the host
of a new game show.

78
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:46,625
Oh, cool!
That's great.

79
00:02:46,667 --> 00:02:48,293
Yeah, yeah, and if I get it,
by day, I'll be

80
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:49,962
( lowers voice ):
Dr. Drake Remoray

81
00:02:50,004 --> 00:02:51,379
but by night, I'll be

82
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:53,924
( loud and excited ):
Joey Tribbiani!

83
00:02:53,966 --> 00:02:56,051
You'll be perfect
for this.

84
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:58,137
That's already your name.

85
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,014
The audition's
in a couple of hours

86
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:02,057
and I don't even understand
the game.

87
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:03,558
Well, do you
want some help?

88
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,977
Really? That would be great.

89
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:06,603
Hey, you guys
could be the contestants.

90
00:03:06,645 --> 00:03:08,396
Awesome.

91
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:10,774
Okay, I guess we can lose
to junior high girls

92
00:03:10,816 --> 00:03:12,109
some other time.

93
00:03:12,151 --> 00:03:13,276
All right--

94
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,987
let's play Bamboozled!

95
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:16,446
Bamboozled?

96
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:17,614
Yeah, isn't that
a cool name?

97
00:03:17,656 --> 00:03:18,740
Yeah.
No.

98
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:20,075
All right.

99
00:03:20,117 --> 00:03:21,326
Uh, okay.

100
00:03:21,368 --> 00:03:23,162
Our first contestant
is Ross Geller.

101
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:24,913
Why don't you tell us
a little bit

102
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:26,081
about yourself, Ross?

103
00:03:26,123 --> 00:03:27,166
Well, uh

104
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,334
I-I'm a
paleontologist.

105
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:31,712
Um, I-I live
in New York.

106
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,505
I have a son, Ben.

107
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:34,715
Uh, hi, Ben.

108
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:35,924
And, uh...

109
00:03:35,966 --> 00:03:37,467
I said
a little bit, Ross.

110
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:39,219
Now, how about you, Chandler?

111
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,013
Well, Joey,
I'm a headhunter.

112
00:03:41,055 --> 00:03:43,348
I hook up
out-of-work Soviet scientists

113
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,266
with rogue Third World nations.

114
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,144
Hi, Rasputin.

115
00:03:47,186 --> 00:03:49,021
Excellent. Let's play
Bamboozled.

116
00:03:49,063 --> 00:03:50,522
Chandler,
you'll go first.

117
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:52,273
"What is the capital
of Colombia?"

118
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:54,068
Bogota.

119
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:56,528
It's "Bagoda,"
but close enough.

120
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:59,156
Uh... now,
oh, now

121
00:03:59,198 --> 00:04:01,282
you can either pass
your turn to Ross

122
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,868
or pick a Wicked
Wango card.

123
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:04,995
What does
a Wicked Wango card do?

124
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:07,122
I should know that.

125
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:09,958
Let's see-- just
one moment, please.

126
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,459
Um... here we are.

127
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,753
"A Wicked Wango card

128
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:15,255
determines whether
you go higher or lower."

129
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:19,634
Higher or lower than what?

130
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:22,470
( phony host voice ):
This is embarrassing.

131
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:24,639
Can you believe
how lame this is?

132
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:27,101
I'm sorry,
I don't believe contestants

133
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:29,352
are allowed
to talk to each other.

134
00:04:34,191 --> 00:04:35,984
Oh, I told the stripper
to be here at 5:00.

135
00:04:36,026 --> 00:04:37,360
That's good, right?

136
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:41,073
You ordered a stripper
for the shower?

137
00:04:41,115 --> 00:04:42,866
That is totally
inappropriate.

138
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:44,868
Why? He's going to be dressed
as a baby.

139
00:04:46,245 --> 00:04:47,955
Oh, hi, Mrs. Green.

140
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:50,665
I'm so glad you
could make it.

141
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:51,833
Yes, thank you so much.

142
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,210
And again,
we're so sorry.

143
00:04:53,252 --> 00:04:55,003
We could not feel worse
about it.

144
00:04:55,045 --> 00:04:56,713
Try.

145
00:04:58,423 --> 00:05:00,341
Oh, there's my little girl.

146
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:01,760
She's still mad.

147
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:02,844
Yeah, I know.

148
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:04,096
Isn't it great--
one less person

149
00:05:04,138 --> 00:05:06,347
we have to make
small talk with?

150
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:09,017
Phoebe, Sandra's mad
at you, too.

151
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:10,852
It doesn't bother you?

152
00:05:10,894 --> 00:05:12,479
Well, we've
apologized twice

153
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,522
and I can't do
any more than that.

154
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:17,192
I know you hate it when
people are mad at you

155
00:05:17,234 --> 00:05:20,112
but, you know, you just
have to be okay with it.

156
00:05:21,113 --> 00:05:22,864
Okay. I can do that.

157
00:05:22,906 --> 00:05:24,032
( chuckling )

158
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:26,076
I got to go powder my ass.

159
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:28,954
Look at that face.

160
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:31,039
Just like when you
were in high school.

161
00:05:31,081 --> 00:05:32,332
If I didn't know better

162
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:34,626
I'd say you were a
cheerleader in trouble.

163
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:35,710
( both chuckling )

164
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:37,004
Come on, let's
get some tea.

165
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,255
My, look at that.

166
00:05:38,297 --> 00:05:39,422
Only three weeks to go.

167
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,258
Now, have you picked
your nanny yet?

168
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:44,094
Now, honey, I don't
want you to just
use your housekeeper

169
00:05:44,136 --> 00:05:45,929
'cause it will just
split her focus.

170
00:05:45,971 --> 00:05:47,055
Oh, well, actually

171
00:05:47,097 --> 00:05:48,556
I'm not going to use a nanny

172
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:50,767
and, uh, I don't even have
a housekeeper.

173
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:52,811
It's like you're
a cave person.

174
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,438
Rachel

175
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,564
you must get a nanny.

176
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:57,983
You don't know
how overwhelming

177
00:05:58,025 --> 00:05:59,151
this is going to be.

178
00:05:59,193 --> 00:06:00,443
I mean, when
you were a baby

179
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,321
I had full-time help--
I had Mrs. Kaye.

180
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:04,572
Mrs. Kaye--
oh, she was sweet.

181
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,241
She taught me Spanish.

182
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:09,203
I actually think
I remember some of it.

183
00:06:09,244 --> 00:06:12,206
Tu madre es loca.

184
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:15,750
Such a sweet woman.

185
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,294
Yeah.

186
00:06:17,336 --> 00:06:20,297
Well, however great she was,
I just can't afford that.

187
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:21,506
Oh, Rachel!

188
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:23,300
What?
I just had the
greatest idea.

189
00:06:23,342 --> 00:06:26,094
I'm going to come
live with you.

190
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:28,889
Wh-Wh-What? What?

191
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:32,559
Oh, I'm so happy
I'm going to do this
for my little girl.

192
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,311
Oh, look at you.

193
00:06:34,353 --> 00:06:37,356
You have tears
in your eyes.

194
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,026
Yes, yes, I do.

195
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,863
All right, Ross,
you're in the lead.

196
00:06:44,905 --> 00:06:46,907
Would you like
to take another question

197
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:48,407
or spin the Wheel of Mayhem?

198
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:51,870
The Wheel has not been
my friend tonight, Joey.

199
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:54,373
Uh... I'll take
another question.

200
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:55,957
Okay. This is going
to be tough.

201
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:57,084
Hold your breath.

202
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,293
It's okay;
I'm ready.

203
00:06:58,335 --> 00:06:59,878
No, dude,
you got to hold your breath

204
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,838
till you're ready
to answer the question.

205
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,590
It's part
of the game.
This is
ridiculous.

206
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:06,176
He's not
going to...
( inhaling loudly )

207
00:07:06,218 --> 00:07:07,344
Okay.

208
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:08,970
"What do you have a fear of

209
00:07:09,012 --> 00:07:10,889
"if you suffer
from this phobia?

210
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:12,724
Tris... ka..."

211
00:07:12,766 --> 00:07:14,475
Holy cow,
that's a big word.

212
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:16,061
"Trisk..."

213
00:07:16,103 --> 00:07:17,520
Seriously,
look at this thing.

214
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,022
Chandler,
how do you say that?

215
00:07:19,064 --> 00:07:20,065
Let me see that.

216
00:07:20,107 --> 00:07:21,358
This one right here.

217
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,151
( high-pitched mumble )

218
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:25,195
"Triskaidekaphobia."

219
00:07:25,237 --> 00:07:28,073
( loud exhale ):
Fear of Triscuits.

220
00:07:28,115 --> 00:07:29,991
No, fear of the number 13.

221
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:31,368
Fear of Triscuits?

222
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:32,535
It's possible.

223
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,996
They have really sharp edges.

224
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:37,832
All right, Chandler,
you're up.

225
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,751
Wait a minute.
I believe I'm entitled

226
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:41,628
to use my Angel Pass
for a free turn.

227
00:07:41,669 --> 00:07:43,088
This game makes no sense!

228
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:44,756
You know,
you're just upset

229
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:46,091
'cause you're losing.

230
00:07:46,133 --> 00:07:47,217
Oh, come on, Ross.

231
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:48,802
I think we're all losers here.

232
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:51,679
All right, Chandler

233
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,307
you can either
spin the wheel

234
00:07:53,348 --> 00:07:54,599
or pick a Google card.

235
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,643
Let me think,
let me think.

236
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:58,312
Oh, uh, I don't care.

237
00:07:58,353 --> 00:07:59,562
( chuckling )

238
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:01,940
You must choose,
Mr. Bing.

239
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:03,691
Either.
It makes no difference.

240
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:06,611
Choose, you jackass.

241
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:08,029
I'll take a card.

242
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:09,323
Okay.

243
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:11,074
You picked
the Gimme card.

244
00:08:11,116 --> 00:08:12,993
You get all of
Ross's points.

245
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:14,535
What?!

246
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:16,997
This game is kind of fun.

247
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:19,333
You don't think
it's a little crazy

248
00:08:19,374 --> 00:08:21,293
that you get
all my points...?

249
00:08:21,335 --> 00:08:23,586
I don't think the contestants

250
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:25,713
are supposed to speak
to each other.

251
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:29,176
Why did you invite my mother?!

252
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,178
What?

253
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:33,013
She wants to move in
with me and Ross

254
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,555
to help take care of the baby.

255
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:35,598
For how long?

256
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,724
Eight weeks.

257
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,268
I mean, I
love my mother

258
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:41,104
but, my God, a
long lunch with
her is taxing.

259
00:08:41,146 --> 00:08:43,023
I personally
would be honored

260
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:45,108
if she wanted
to live with me.

261
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:46,360
She can't hear you.

262
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,571
You guys, come on,
what am I going to do?

263
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:53,908
Well, if you don't want
your mother to move in with you

264
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:54,951
just tell her.

265
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:56,161
You're right. You're right.

266
00:08:56,203 --> 00:08:57,536
I mean,
I'm about to have a baby.

267
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,164
I can tell my mother

268
00:08:59,206 --> 00:09:00,915
that I don't want her
to be sleeping on my couch.

269
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:03,418
Oh, my God, she's going to want
to sleep in my bed with me.

270
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:04,585
This cannot happen.

271
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:05,879
That's right.
That is right.

272
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,297
You go over there
and tell her

273
00:09:07,339 --> 00:09:09,049
you do not want her
to live with you.

274
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,425
Do not take no
for an answer.

275
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:11,510
Okay.

276
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:12,969
This is great.

277
00:09:13,011 --> 00:09:15,472
Now she's going
to be mad at Rachel.

278
00:09:15,514 --> 00:09:18,850
You know what?
And I'm just going
to swoop in there

279
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:21,520
and be like the daughter
she never had.

280
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:25,106
I have new respect
for Chandler.

281
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:31,112
All right, everybody,
it's time to open the presents!

282
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:32,613
Yes, yes, and I think

283
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:35,116
that the first gift
that Rachel opens

284
00:09:35,158 --> 00:09:37,494
should be from the
grandmother of the baby.

285
00:09:37,536 --> 00:09:39,704
Because you're the
most important person

286
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:40,830
in this room.

287
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:42,249
And in the world.

288
00:09:44,209 --> 00:09:45,710
Well, uh, I don't have a gift

289
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:47,670
because I wasn't invited
until the last minute

290
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,172
but thank you so much, dear

291
00:09:49,214 --> 00:09:51,007
for bringing that
to everybody's attention.

292
00:09:54,593 --> 00:09:56,804
How about
you less important people?

293
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,473
Let's open your presents.

294
00:09:58,515 --> 00:10:02,727
Hey, Mom, that's okay
that you didn't get me a gift.

295
00:10:02,769 --> 00:10:04,645
Well, I kind of did. Me.

296
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,106
Eight weeks of me.

297
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:08,442
Yeah. Okay, see, Mom,
the truth is

298
00:10:08,483 --> 00:10:10,151
I can do this on my own.

299
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:11,694
Sweetheart

300
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:13,654
I know you're going
to be a terrific mom.

301
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:15,323
I just think you
need a little help

302
00:10:15,365 --> 00:10:16,699
especially at the beginning.

303
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:18,410
But, Mom, I really know
what I'm doing.

304
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:19,494
I can handle this.

305
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:21,580
Really? Remember Twinkles?

306
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,830
He was a hamster.

307
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:25,417
I am not going
to vacuum up my baby.

308
00:10:25,459 --> 00:10:26,667
Okay

309
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:27,752
come on, Rach.

310
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:28,920
It's present time.

311
00:10:28,962 --> 00:10:30,547
You know, you're the glue

312
00:10:30,589 --> 00:10:32,715
holding this whole party
together.

313
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,968
It's kind of falling apart here.

314
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:37,262
Ooh, look.

315
00:10:37,304 --> 00:10:38,637
Wow.

316
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,640
This is from
your friends at work.

317
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:41,849
Ooh! My gosh!

318
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:43,268
Oh, wow!

319
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:46,687
Oh, I know what this is.

320
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:48,898
Wait a minute.

321
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,526
That can't be right.

322
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:53,861
Is that a beer bong
for a baby?

323
00:10:55,614 --> 00:10:58,366
Darling, that's
a breast pump.

324
00:10:58,408 --> 00:11:00,076
( coughing chuckle )

325
00:11:00,118 --> 00:11:02,537
Did I say
I was done guessing?

326
00:11:02,579 --> 00:11:05,290
Okay, thank you for that.

327
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:06,625
Ooh, wow.

328
00:11:06,665 --> 00:11:08,126
What's this?

329
00:11:08,168 --> 00:11:09,503
It's a Diaper Genie.

330
00:11:09,544 --> 00:11:11,754
Oh, it dispenses
clean diapers.

331
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:13,965
No, it's where
you put the dirty ones.

332
00:11:14,007 --> 00:11:15,133
Well, that's gross.

333
00:11:15,175 --> 00:11:16,675
Why don't you
just take it outside

334
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,011
and throw it
in a Dumpster?

335
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:20,054
Oh, you're going to do
that ten times a day?

336
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,599
What, it goes
ten times a day?!

337
00:11:22,641 --> 00:11:26,186
What are we feeding
this baby, Indian food?

338
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:29,523
No, dear, that's
what babies do.

339
00:11:29,564 --> 00:11:31,525
Rachel,
listen to your mother.

340
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:32,859
She is very smart.

341
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:37,364
Plus, what are you
planning on doing
with the baby

342
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:39,949
while you're trotting
out to the garbage
ten times a day?

343
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:41,159
I don't know.

344
00:11:41,201 --> 00:11:42,701
Leave it on the changing table?

345
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:44,120
( women gasping )

346
00:11:44,162 --> 00:11:46,289
What? What'd I do?
What'd I do?

347
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:48,333
You can't leave
a baby alone.

348
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:49,543
( sputtering )

349
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:51,545
Of course.
I know that.

350
00:11:51,586 --> 00:11:54,589
I mean, of course
you never leave a baby alone.

351
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:56,883
( laughing ):
She wouldn't be safe.

352
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,301
You know, not as safe

353
00:11:58,343 --> 00:12:00,928
as she would be with me,
the baby dummy.

354
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,889
Ooh, God,
okay, you know what?

355
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:04,182
Opening the presents

356
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:05,642
is a little overwhelming
right now

357
00:12:05,684 --> 00:12:07,561
so I think, um,
I'm just going to maybe

358
00:12:07,602 --> 00:12:09,354
open them all a little bit later

359
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:12,273
but thank you all for coming
and for these beautiful gifts

360
00:12:12,315 --> 00:12:13,858
and this basket is beautiful.

361
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,776
It's actually a bassinet.

362
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,780
Okay, Mommy,
don't ever leave me.

363
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:26,996
"In what John Huston film
would you hear this line--

364
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:28,707
"'Badges? We don't need
no stinking badges'?

365
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:30,208
Treasure of
the Sierra Madre!

366
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,959
Correct. There's
a possible backwards bonus.

367
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:34,671
Madre Sierra the of Treasure!

368
00:12:34,713 --> 00:12:35,880
Yes!

369
00:12:35,922 --> 00:12:37,340
I'd like to go up
the Ladder of Chance

370
00:12:37,382 --> 00:12:38,508
to the Golden
Mud Hut, please.

371
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:39,718
Wise choice.
How many rungs?

372
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:40,719
Six.

373
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:42,303
( cackles like monkey )

374
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:44,389
That noise
can only mean one thing.

375
00:12:44,431 --> 00:12:47,183
Hungry monkey! Ha!
Hungry monkey.

376
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:48,809
I'd like a Wicked Wango card.

377
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:49,810
Okay.

378
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:51,396
It's an audio question.

379
00:12:51,438 --> 00:12:53,356
"Name this television
theme song."

380
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:55,692
( sings I Dream
of Jeannie theme )

381
00:12:55,734 --> 00:12:56,693
Oh...

382
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:57,985
Oh. Oh, my God.

383
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:59,529
Okay, I know this.
Give me a second.

384
00:12:59,571 --> 00:13:00,739
Tell it to the Time Turtle!

385
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:01,864
Shut up!

386
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:03,450
I Dream of Jeannie!
Yes.

387
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:04,451
You're back
in the lead.

388
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:05,577
I'd like
to spin the wheel.

389
00:13:05,619 --> 00:13:07,161
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat...

390
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,246
tat... tat... tat...

391
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:10,039
tat... tat...

392
00:13:10,081 --> 00:13:11,832
tat...

393
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,585
Oh, come on!
Oh, come on!

394
00:13:13,627 --> 00:13:15,545
Uh, Super-Speedy Speed round.

395
00:13:15,587 --> 00:13:16,879
Is there
a hopping bonus?

396
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:17,922
Of course.

397
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:23,720
"Who invented bifocals?"

398
00:13:23,762 --> 00:13:25,388
Ben Franklin.
Correct.

399
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:27,724
"Which monarch has ruled
Great Britain the longest?"

400
00:13:27,766 --> 00:13:29,309
Queen Victoria.
Correct
again.

401
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:31,561
But you forgot to switch legs
between questions

402
00:13:31,603 --> 00:13:35,231
so no Hopping Bonus.
Oh! No! Every time!

403
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:38,318
Now, over to Chandler.

404
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:39,486
I'd like a Google card.

405
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:40,737
Are you sure?

406
00:13:40,779 --> 00:13:41,820
Yes.

407
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,281
No!

408
00:13:43,323 --> 00:13:44,991
Google!

409
00:13:46,451 --> 00:13:47,494
Oh, my God.

410
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,120
Congratulations, Ross.

411
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:51,830
Because, Chandler,
you've been Bamboozled!

412
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:52,666
No!

413
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:53,874
Yes!

414
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,877
This is the
best game ever!

415
00:13:58,630 --> 00:14:00,465
So, um, you're going
to stay with me

416
00:14:00,507 --> 00:14:01,675
as long as I need you?

417
00:14:01,716 --> 00:14:02,967
Of course I am.

418
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:04,719
Oh, Mom, I swear,
I'm not an idiot.

419
00:14:04,761 --> 00:14:07,472
I read all kinds
of books on pregnancy
and giving birth

420
00:14:07,514 --> 00:14:09,182
but I just didn't think
to read the part

421
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:10,767
about what to do
when the baby comes.

422
00:14:10,809 --> 00:14:13,894
And-and... guess what--
the baby's coming

423
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:15,271
and I don't know what to do.

424
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:16,439
Oh.

425
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:18,274
Could I throw up
in my Diaper Genie?

426
00:14:18,316 --> 00:14:22,362
Oh, sweetie, you're
going to be fine.

427
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:24,113
Wait, where you going?
Where you going?

428
00:14:24,155 --> 00:14:25,782
I'm going to
the bathroom.
Oh, okay.

429
00:14:25,824 --> 00:14:27,158
Now, don't worry.

430
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,661
Everything's
going to be okay.

431
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:33,832
It is going to be okay.

432
00:14:37,836 --> 00:14:39,170
Worth a shot.

433
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:43,090
Hey.
Hey.

434
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:44,884
Why are you all
red and sweaty?

435
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,678
I just Bamboozled Chandler.

436
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:53,017
Which is not a sexual thing.

437
00:14:54,853 --> 00:14:56,354
That was a quick shower.

438
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:57,814
Not if you were here.

439
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,108
Wow, looks like we got
a lot of good stuff.

440
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,610
Oh, we did.

441
00:15:02,652 --> 00:15:04,487
But my mom got us
the greatest gift of all.

442
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:06,698
A Play-Doh barber shop?

443
00:15:07,699 --> 00:15:08,991
No.

444
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:11,994
She's going to live
with us for eight weeks.

445
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,621
Wh-What?

446
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:16,583
Yeah, she's going to help us
take care of the baby. Whoo.

447
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:20,044
You're not serious.

448
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:22,589
I mean, she's
a very nice woman

449
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,466
but there's no way we can
take eight weeks of her.

450
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:26,801
She'll drive us
totally crazy...

451
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:27,926
Hi, Ross.

452
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:29,846
Hey, roomie!

453
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:36,977
Hey, Joey, hi.

454
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,938
I'm Ray, I'm the
producer of the show.

455
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:41,107
( phony host voice ):
It's a pleasure
to meet you, Ray.

456
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,610
And this is
Duncan and Erin.

457
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,236
They're going help us out
with the audition.

458
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:46,738
So, let's get
the camera rolling.

459
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:48,364
Righty-o, Ray.

460
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:50,909
Whenever you're ready.

461
00:15:50,949 --> 00:15:53,453
Hello, I'm Joey Tribbiani.

462
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:55,705
Let's play Bamboozled.

463
00:15:55,747 --> 00:15:57,707
Erin, you get
the first question.

464
00:15:57,749 --> 00:16:00,585
"In hockey,
who is known as the Great One?"

465
00:16:00,627 --> 00:16:02,169
Wayne Gretzky.
Correct.

466
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:04,505
Now, would you like
to pick a Wicked Wango card

467
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:06,090
or spin the Wheel of Mayhem?

468
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:09,427
Uh, Joey, didn't your agents
give you the revised rules?

469
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:10,929
We've eliminated all that.

470
00:16:10,969 --> 00:16:12,513
No wheel, no cards.

471
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:14,181
Wh-Why?

472
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:17,017
Uh, well, the game
was too complicated

473
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,938
and research showed
people didn't follow it.

474
00:16:19,978 --> 00:16:21,564
What's complicated?

475
00:16:21,606 --> 00:16:23,608
You spin the Wheel of Mayhem
to go up the Ladder of Chance

476
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,652
you go past the Mud Hut
through the Rainbow Ring

477
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,320
to get to the Golden Monkey

478
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:30,239
you yank his tail, and boom,
you're in Paradise Pond.

479
00:16:30,281 --> 00:16:31,240
Yeah.

480
00:16:31,282 --> 00:16:33,033
All that's gone.

481
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:36,370
It's basically just a simple
question-and-answer game now.

482
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,247
Well, what's fun about that?

483
00:16:38,289 --> 00:16:40,667
You expect me to be the host
of some boring game

484
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:43,503
that's just people standing
around answering questions?

485
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:46,464
Well, there'll be women in
bikinis holding up the scores.

486
00:16:46,506 --> 00:16:48,675
Let's play Bamboozled.

487
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:52,386
And all those dinosaur
knickknacks you have

488
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:55,556
Ross, I thought they might be
more at home in the garage.

489
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:57,558
Well, we don't
have a garage.

490
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,852
Did I say garage?

491
00:16:58,893 --> 00:17:00,353
I meant garbage.

492
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:03,857
You know what,
Mrs. Green

493
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:05,984
maybe it's not
absolutely vital

494
00:17:06,024 --> 00:17:07,527
that you live with us.

495
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:09,988
But Rachel needs help
with the baby.

496
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:11,489
I do, I really do.

497
00:17:11,531 --> 00:17:13,324
I don't know anything.

498
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:15,201
I'm sure that's not true.

499
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:16,953
Oh, no?

500
00:17:16,995 --> 00:17:18,788
Pheebs, Monica,
do I know anything
about babies?

501
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:19,956
Nope, not
a thing.

502
00:17:19,998 --> 00:17:21,499
It's frightening.

503
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:22,750
Well, you know what

504
00:17:22,792 --> 00:17:24,794
even if she doesn't
know anything, I do.

505
00:17:24,836 --> 00:17:27,881
I have a son, and his mother
and I didn't live together

506
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:29,465
and whenever he was with me

507
00:17:29,507 --> 00:17:31,926
I took care of him
all the time, by myself.

508
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:33,928
That's true.

509
00:17:33,970 --> 00:17:35,137
You do have another child.

510
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:36,138
Yeah.

511
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,765
With another woman.

512
00:17:37,807 --> 00:17:40,727
Have you no control, Ross?

513
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,398
That's a different issue.

514
00:17:47,107 --> 00:17:49,569
The point is,
when the baby comes

515
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:53,740
I will be there to feed her
and bathe her and change her

516
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:56,743
and, more than that, I want
to do all those things.

517
00:17:58,285 --> 00:18:00,705
Well, then you really don't
need me to live with you.

518
00:18:00,747 --> 00:18:01,789
Yes!

519
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:06,044
Yes, you're going
to be so missed.

520
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:08,922
You're going to be
a great father.

521
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:10,631
Well, you're going to be
a wonderful grandma.

522
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:12,675
Hello?

523
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:15,929
I still don't know
what the hell I'm doing.

524
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:18,765
Oh, come on, every
first-time mother
feels that way.

525
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,641
You'll... you're going
to pick it up.

526
00:18:20,683 --> 00:18:22,268
Hey, you will.

527
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:25,438
Look, you know when you
first came to the city

528
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:28,107
you were this spoiled
helpless little girl

529
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:31,069
who still used daddy's
credit cards, remember?

530
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:33,654
I hope you're going
somewhere with this.

531
00:18:33,696 --> 00:18:35,322
Look at you, would you?

532
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:37,283
You're this big executive.

533
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:38,451
You are much
more capable

534
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:40,160
than you give
yourself credit for.

535
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:43,831
I have no doubt you're going
to be an incredible mother.

536
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:45,875
Really?

537
00:18:45,917 --> 00:18:47,919
I'm telling you.

538
00:18:47,961 --> 00:18:49,796
Thank you.

539
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:54,174
All right, you two

540
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,426
I'm going
to get going.

541
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,053
Oh, no, no,
sweetheart.

542
00:18:57,095 --> 00:18:58,054
You stay put.

543
00:18:58,096 --> 00:18:59,221
I'll let myself out.

544
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:00,640
It's like I'm not here.

545
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:01,975
Which I almost wasn't.

546
00:19:02,016 --> 00:19:04,018
( laughs loudly )

547
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:07,229
You're still so funny.
It's so funny.

548
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:08,982
What do I do?

549
00:19:09,023 --> 00:19:10,733
Nothing.

550
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:13,319
You have apologized to her,
like, a million times

551
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,655
and she's been nothing
but terrible to you.

552
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,156
And don't forget

553
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:19,325
you just threw
her daughter a lovely

554
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:21,911
albeit slightly boring,
shower.

555
00:19:21,953 --> 00:19:25,498
And she hasn't even
thanked you for it.

556
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,875
You know what, you're right.

557
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:29,251
Yeah, I mean, if you want

558
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,670
to say anything to her,
I'd tell her off.

559
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:31,712
Really?

560
00:19:31,754 --> 00:19:32,880
Uh-huh.

561
00:19:33,923 --> 00:19:36,634
Okay, I will.

562
00:19:36,676 --> 00:19:38,052
Mrs. Green.

563
00:19:39,053 --> 00:19:40,178
Mrs. Green.

564
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,764
It is rude to
leave a party

565
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:43,975
without saying
good-bye to the host.

566
00:19:44,017 --> 00:19:46,268
And also, when someone
apologizes to you

567
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:48,562
the decent thing to do
is to accept it.

568
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:51,190
Because what I did to you,
it wasn't on purpose

569
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:55,235
but what you're doing to me now,
it's just plain spiteful.

570
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,821
Spiteful?
That's right.

571
00:19:56,863 --> 00:19:59,157
Maybe it's time you
took a good hard look

572
00:19:59,197 --> 00:20:00,700
in the mirror, young lady.

573
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,702
Old lady.

574
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:04,537
Lady.

575
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:06,706
Wrap it up, wrap it up,
wrap it up.

576
00:20:08,041 --> 00:20:11,127
So, whenever you're
ready to apologize to me

577
00:20:11,169 --> 00:20:12,461
I will forgive you.

578
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:13,587
Good day.

579
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:20,219
I can't feel my legs.

580
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,971
But you were fantastic.

581
00:20:22,013 --> 00:20:23,848
I'm so proud of you.

582
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:24,891
Yeah?

583
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:27,060
I'm proud of me, too.

584
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:28,394
You should be.

585
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:29,729
Could you get me
something to drink?

586
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:30,771
You got it.

587
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:32,398
Okay.

588
00:20:32,439 --> 00:20:33,649
Mrs. Green!

589
00:20:33,691 --> 00:20:35,193
Okay, I'm really sorry!
I apologize!

590
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,194
If you could...

591
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:37,235
( screams )

592
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:38,946
( thudding )

593
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:40,907
Okay, I bit my tongue...

594
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:45,285
( lisping ):
but I'm thtill really thorry!

595
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:53,920
Okay, I'm ready.

596
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,046
You sure?
Yes.

597
00:20:55,088 --> 00:20:56,130
I've done my studying

598
00:20:56,172 --> 00:20:57,673
and I really know my stuff.

599
00:20:57,715 --> 00:20:58,841
All right, then.

600
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:04,638
Rachel Green,
let's play Bamboozled.

601
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,683
"How do you test the temperature
of the baby's bath water?"

602
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:08,976
Uh, put your elbow in it.

603
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:10,228
Excellent.

604
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:11,729
"How do you put
a baby down for a nap?"

605
00:21:11,771 --> 00:21:14,774
Full, dry, on it's back,
and no loose covers.

606
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:15,775
That's correct.

607
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:17,526
This is an audio question.

608
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:20,071
"What do you do
when the baby makes this sound?"

609
00:21:20,113 --> 00:21:21,739
( high-pitched crying )

610
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:27,620
Check if it's wet,
check if it's hungry, burp it.

611
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:28,996
Excellent! Excellent!

612
00:21:29,038 --> 00:21:30,623
Now, now, do you
want another question

613
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:32,833
or a Wicked Wango card?

614
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:34,127
A card, a card, I pick a card.

615
00:21:34,168 --> 00:21:37,713
Oh, I'm sorry,
you've been Bamboozled.

616
00:21:37,755 --> 00:21:40,340
You're going
to be a terrible mother.

617
00:21:42,718 --> 00:21:46,430
( phony host voice ):
I've lost sight
of why we're doing this.

618
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:52,436
